Third-party data
----------------
seeds/casino_profiles.json is derived from the CaSiNo dataset:
  Kushal Chawla, Jaysa Ramirez, Rene Clever, Gale Lucas, Jonathan May, Jonathan Gratch.
  "CaSiNo: A Corpus of Campsite Negotiation Dialogues for Automatic Negotiation Systems." NAACL 2021.
  https://github.com/kushalchawla/CaSiNo (data/casino.json, commit 2f6ed4a6a55110152a7699fbaa8150d6036314be)
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Modified: we keep only, per annotated participant, the counts of the annotated persuasion-strategy labels.
  No dialogue text is included. The tournament uses these profiles as speaking-style hints for simulated
  homeowners; the original corpus is about campsite supplies, not home services.

Not used: CraigslistBargain (dataset license unknown; Craigslist terms forbid derivative works) and
Deal or No Deal (CC BY-NC).

Models
------
Agent decisions run on NVIDIA Nemotron models served by Nebius Token Factory (Nemotron 3 Super and Nano: NVIDIA
Nemotron Open Model License; Nemotron 3 Ultra, 3.5 Lightning and 3.5 Super-VL: OpenMDW-1.1). Model weights are not
redistributed here. The simulated buyers in the evaluation are played by a non-NVIDIA open model on Token Factory.
